  "verbalization": "Flunarizine exhibits a bidirectional relationship with Cyp2a6, as evidenced by its binding to Cyp2b6 and Cyp2a6's participation in metabolic processes. The evidence suggests that Flunarizine may influence Cyp2a6 through its interaction with Cyp2b6, which in turn is involved in nicotine metabolism. This implies that Flunarizine could modulate Cyp2a6 activity indirectly, potentially affecting the metabolism of nicotine or other substrates. The shared involvement of Cyp2a6 in different metabolic pathways highlights a possible functional overlap, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Cyp2a6 in metabolic regulation, with Flunarizine potentially acting as a modulator of its activity.",
